// JSON convenience operations are moving into the language in rfd#43.
//
// The compiler-owned toJSON() and parseJSON<T>() methods provide the typed,
// round-trippable surface. This package is intentionally transitional: the
// former untyped parse/stringify helpers are removed rather than reintroduced
// with a dishonest top type or an unsafe JSON.parse wrapper.
//
// Higher-level helpers such as flatten-for-display, sorted keys, and pretty
// printing will be added here on top of the language methods.
